Writes sign-in screens into this app: an email-and-code sign-in screen and a "where you're signed in" screen, on the headless auth client, so they work on the web and in native apps.

Also adds `[auth]` to leptoskit.toml, the leptoskit features the screens use, the file router's routes when the app has one, and the server's sign-in module when it has a server and a database. Running it again changes nothing; a file you've edited is kept.

Usage: leptoskit generate auth [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --force
          Replace files that differ from the templates

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
